+# Task: Add renderSummary and --summary flag to frai-gate
+
+## Implementation Steps
+
+- [x] **Step 1**: Add `renderSummary(result: GateResult): string` function to `src/gate/report.ts`
+  - Format: `<VERDICT> <answered>/<total>`
+  - Total is always 7 (GATE_CHECKS.length)
+  - Answered = count of GATE_CHECKS with no block-severity finding
+  - If block findings exist for GATE_CHECKS, append `: ` and their checkIds in GATE_CHECKS order, comma-separated
+  - Example: `BLOCK 5/7: evaluation, transparency`
+  - Special case: if structure finding exists, return `BLOCK 0/7: structure`
+  - Export the function
+
+- [x] **Step 2**: Add `--summary` flag handling to `cmdCheck()` in `src/cli.ts`
+  - Add logic to check for `--summary` flag
+  - Print only the summary line when `--summary` is present
+  - Exit codes unchanged (1 on BLOCK, 0 otherwise)
+  - `--json` flag takes priority if both are given
+
+- [x] **Step 3**: Update HELP text in `src/cli.ts`
+  - Document the new `--summary` flag in the `frai-gate check` command description
+  - Document its behavior and priority vs `--json`
+
+- [x] **Step 4**: Add tests for `renderSummary()` in `src/gate/report.test.ts` (create if needed)
+  - Test PASS case with no findings
+  - Test WARN case with warnings only
+  - Test BLOCK case with block findings from multiple checks
+  - Test BLOCK with structure finding
+  - Test ordering of check IDs matches GATE_CHECKS order
+
+- [x] **Step 5**: Build and run tests
+  - Run `pnpm --filter frai-gate build`
+  - Run `pnpm --filter frai-gate test`
+  - Verify all tests pass
+
+## Completion Criteria
+
+- ✅ All checkboxes above are ticked
+- ✅ `renderSummary()` function is exported and works correctly
+  - ✅ Returns `PASS 7/7` for specs with no findings
+  - ✅ Returns `WARN 7/7` for specs with only warnings
+  - ✅ Returns `BLOCK N/7: check1, check2` for specs with block findings
+  - ✅ Returns `BLOCK 0/7: structure` when gate section is missing
+  - ✅ Check IDs are listed in GATE_CHECKS order
+- ✅ `--summary` flag works and prioritizes correctly with `--json`
+  - ✅ `--json` takes priority when both flags are provided
+  - ✅ Exit code is correct (1 for BLOCK, 0 for PASS/WARN)
+- ✅ HELP text is updated
+- ✅ Tests pass (19 tests: 8 new + 11 existing)
+- ✅ Build succeeds
